/* The buyer's note on an order that ships nothing (round BC, SQL part 283): `orders.buyer_note`, what the buyer wrote for the shop at the website's checkout, or in an imported theme's cart ("Add order note", Shopify's cart note), kept on every line of a basket of downloads (lib/checkout/fulfil-cart-session.ts). A cart that ships already keeps it on its checkout (`commerce_checkouts.buyer_note`, part 78), so this is the same words for the rest: plain text, line breaks kept, at most 1000 characters (lib/checkout/site-checkout.ts orderNote). The order page shows it (app/app/orders/order-detail.tsx, read by app/api/app/orders/[id]/activity) and the seller's sale email lists it. Adds one column, empty on every order already there; changes no rows. Written by the server only. Until it runs the order is written as before, the note goes only into the seller's email, and the order page shows none. Safe to run again. */
DO $do$ BEGIN IF to_regclass('public.orders') IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'order buyer note: orders is not there yet.'; RETURN; END IF; ALTER TABLE public.orders ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS buyer_note text; ALTER TABLE public.orders DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS orders_buyer_note_length; ALTER TABLE public.orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_buyer_note_length CHECK (buyer_note IS NULL OR length(buyer_note) <= 1000) NOT VALID; END $do$;
notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
